    "limitations": [
      "Count is a finite canonical unsigned u64 atom, not the arbitrary state tree admitted by the canonical outer action layer. Nil is canonical zero; padded, negative, oversized and pair counts reject.",
      "StateTruth is the improper pair (ephemeral . count), while the exact argument environment is a proper list. Arbitrary ephemeral atom bytes and improper tree tails are preserved. This is the default strict typed ABI, not a raw whole-environment export.",
      "Each action expects nil action_solution after its fixed arguments are curried. Extra arguments and improper argument tails reject; the canonical outer module may ignore other unselected wire data.",
      "PublicKey checks exactly 48 bytes, not curve membership or signing authority. Actual aggregate signatures are checked by the simulator/consensus lane, separately from raw VM vectors.",
      "Reset uses the fixed 32-byte intent chialisp-oxide/counter/reset:v1!. Increment then reset and reset then increment may both be authorized and produce different states; no complete-batch or action-order authorization is claimed.",
      "Canonical SDK host modules have their own published provenance and licenses. Their composition does not mean the outer action layer, finalizer or singleton was implemented in Rust.",
      "Counter tests do not complete issue #14: the registry/slot and actual slot double-spend milestone remains separate. No BLS theorem, live deployment, compiler-preservation proof or production-readiness claim follows."
    ],
